---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Catalog from '../components/Catalog.astro';
import { games, cleanroom } from '../lib/catalog';
const list = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'ItemList', name: 'Decomp Games',
  itemListElement: games.map((g, i) => ({ '@type': 'ListItem', position: i + 1, name: g.title, url: new URL(`/games/${g.id}/`, Astro.site) })),
};
---
<Layout>
  <Catalog />
  <section class="card prose">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">What you are playing</h2>
    <p>Decompilation projects turn a game's machine code back into source that can be rebuilt for new platforms, including the web. The {cleanroom.length} clean-room builds here go a step further: the game logic runs from decompiled or rewritten code, and every texture, model skin and sound has been regenerated, so nothing from the retail release is shipped. <a href="/clean-room/">How the clean room works</a>.</p>
    <p>Connect a controller and it is picked up automatically. On a phone or tablet, on-screen controls appear when no controller is connected. Every game is free, and nothing needs installing.</p>
  </section>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(list).replace(/</g, '\\u003c')} />
</Layout>
